{
  "info": {
    "name": "UnclogMe - GDO Online Reporting Bot API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Test harness for the GDO Online Reporting bot API (Line Item 27).\n\nThe bot reads a QUEUE of code-27 visits to report online on the Miami-Dade DERM portal, and POSTs a RESULT per visit. Both endpoints are live Supabase Edge Functions.\n\n## Setup (once) - no environment needed\nRight-click this collection -> Edit -> Variables tab -> paste your bot key into rpaBotKey's CURRENT VALUE column -> Save. The value lives in Supabase/.env as RPA_BOT_KEY (never commit it). Auth is one header x-rpa-key set at the collection level, so every request uses it automatically. (An optional 'UnclogMe - RPA (Prod)' environment is also included if you prefer keys there; if you use it, it overrides the collection value.)\n\n## How to test\nRun top to bottom. Start with '1. Queue > Queue - dry-run': it returns real historical code-27 visits and captures the first visit_id into a variable the Result requests reuse. Then run the '2. Result' requests (they send dry_run:true, so they are recorded separately and NEVER affect the live queue or what customers/apps see). '3. Validation' shows the endpoint rejecting bad input.\n\nNotes: the LIVE queue is empty until launch. Result writes create harmless dry_run rows in our log table; clear them anytime, they are invisible to the live pipeline. There is no 'SUCCESS needs confirmation' test here on purpose: that rule (and the double-file guards) apply only to LIVE reports; a dry-run SUCCESS is a test and is deliberately exempt, so it cannot be shown against dry-run data (it is verified on the live path in our own suite)."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "apikey",
    "apikey": [
      {
        "key": "key",
        "value": "x-rpa-key",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "value",
        "value": "{{rpaBotKey}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "in",
        "value": "header",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://wbasvhvvismukaqdnouk.supabase.co/functions/v1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "rpaBotKey",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "dryRunVisitId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "dryRunManifestId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Queue (read) - no side effects",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Queue - dry-run (START HERE)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-queue?mode=dryrun",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-queue"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "mode",
                  "value": "dryrun"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Up to 25 REAL historical code-27 visits to report, keyed by visit_id, each with client + service fields, gdo_number, and 4h signed document URLs. Captures the first visit_id/manifest_id for the Result requests. Read-only."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('mode = dryrun', () => pm.expect(j.mode).to.eql('dryrun'));",
                  "pm.test('reports is an array', () => pm.expect(j.reports).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "if (j.reports && j.reports.length) {",
                  "  const r = j.reports[0];",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('dryRunVisitId', r.visit_id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('dryRunManifestId', r.manifest_id);",
                  "  pm.test('report keyed by visit_id, has gdo + signed docs', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(r.visit_id, 'visit_id').to.be.a('number');",
                  "    pm.expect(r, 'gdo_number').to.have.property('gdo_number');",
                  "    pm.expect(r.documents, 'documents.address').to.have.property('address');",
                  "  });",
                  "  console.log('Captured dryRunVisitId=' + r.visit_id + '  (' + r.client_code + ' ' + r.client_name + ', service_date ' + r.service_date + ')');",
                  "} else { console.warn('No dry-run reports returned.'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Queue - live",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-queue",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-queue"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The real live queue of code-27 visits awaiting their online report. Empty (count 0) until launch. A visit stays here until the county confirms its report. Read-only."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('mode = live', () => pm.expect(j.mode).to.eql('live'));",
                  "console.log('Live queue count = ' + j.count + '  (0 until launch: only code-27 visits serviced on/after the cutoff appear).');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Result (write) - dry-run safe",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Report result - retryable failure",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-result",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-result"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs a retryable failure (e.g. portal timeout) for the captured visit. Fresh GUID run_id each send. dry_run:true keeps it out of the live pipeline. Expect 201.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"visit_id\": {{dryRunVisitId}},\n  \"manifest_id\": {{dryRunManifestId}},\n  \"run_id\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"status\": \"ERROR_PORTAL_TIMEOUT\",\n  \"retryable\": true,\n  \"attempted_at\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"failure_reason\": \"Postman test - portal timed out\",\n  \"screenshot_missing_reason\": \"no screenshot in test\",\n  \"dry_run\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Run \"Queue - dry-run\" first to capture a visit', function () {",
                  "  const v = pm.collectionVariables.get('dryRunVisitId');",
                  "  pm.expect(v, 'dryRunVisitId (run the dry-run queue first)').to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('recorded (201 new or 200 dedupe)', () => pm.expect([200,201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "pm.test('recorded flag true', () => pm.expect(j.recorded).to.eql(true));",
                  "console.log('recorded id=' + j.id + '  deduped=' + j.deduped);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Report result - SUCCESS + screenshot",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-result",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-result"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs a confirmed report with portal_confirmation and a tiny base64 JPEG screenshot - exercises the private evidence bucket. dry_run:true. Expect 201. In production the bot sends the real portal screenshot bytes here.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"visit_id\": {{dryRunVisitId}},\n  \"manifest_id\": {{dryRunManifestId}},\n  \"run_id\": \"succ-{{$guid}}\",\n  \"status\": \"SUCCESS\",\n  \"retryable\": false,\n  \"attempted_at\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"portal_confirmation\": \"TEST-CONF-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"screenshot\": \"/9j/4AAQSkZJRgAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICAgICD/2Q==\",\n  \"dry_run\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Run \"Queue - dry-run\" first to capture a visit', function () {",
                  "  const v = pm.collectionVariables.get('dryRunVisitId');",
                  "  pm.expect(v, 'dryRunVisitId (run the dry-run queue first)').to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('recorded (201 new or 200 dedupe)', () => pm.expect([200,201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "pm.test('recorded flag true', () => pm.expect(j.recorded).to.eql(true));",
                  "console.log('recorded id=' + j.id + '  deduped=' + j.deduped);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Report result - dedupe demo (send twice)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-result",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-result"
              ]
            },
            "description": "FIXED run_id 'postman-dedupe-1'. Send once -> 201 {deduped:false}, again -> 200 {deduped:true}: idempotency on (visit_id, run_id) so a retried POST never double-records. (If you already ran it, both are 200 until the dry_run rows are cleared.)",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"visit_id\": {{dryRunVisitId}},\n  \"run_id\": \"postman-dedupe-1\",\n  \"status\": \"ERROR_PORTAL_TIMEOUT\",\n  \"retryable\": true,\n  \"attempted_at\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"screenshot_missing_reason\": \"dedupe demo\",\n  \"dry_run\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Run \"Queue - dry-run\" first to capture a visit', function () {",
                  "  const v = pm.collectionVariables.get('dryRunVisitId');",
                  "  pm.expect(v, 'dryRunVisitId (run the dry-run queue first)').to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 or 201', () => pm.expect([200,201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "console.log(pm.response.code === 201 ? 'First send -> 201 recorded (deduped=false)' : 'Repeat send -> 200 deduped=' + j.deduped);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Validation (expected 4xx)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Bad run_id -> 400",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-result",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-result"
              ]
            },
            "description": "run_id 'bad/slash' contains '/', rejected because run_id becomes part of a storage object key. Expect 400.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"visit_id\": {{dryRunVisitId}},\n  \"run_id\": \"bad/slash\",\n  \"status\": \"ERROR_PORTAL_TIMEOUT\",\n  \"retryable\": true,\n  \"attempted_at\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"screenshot_missing_reason\": \"x\",\n  \"dry_run\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Run \"Queue - dry-run\" first to capture a visit', function () {",
                  "  const v = pm.collectionVariables.get('dryRunVisitId');",
                  "  pm.expect(v, 'dryRunVisitId (run the dry-run queue first)').to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('400 rejected', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('error names run_id', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include('run_id'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Unknown field -> 400",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-result",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-result"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sends an unexpected body field; unknown fields are rejected so a typo cannot silently no-op. Expect 400.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"visit_id\": {{dryRunVisitId}},\n  \"run_id\": \"unknown-{{$guid}}\",\n  \"status\": \"ERROR_PORTAL_TIMEOUT\",\n  \"retryable\": true,\n  \"attempted_at\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"screenshot_missing_reason\": \"x\",\n  \"dry_run\": true,\n  \"totally_made_up_field\": 1\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Run \"Queue - dry-run\" first to capture a visit', function () {",
                  "  const v = pm.collectionVariables.get('dryRunVisitId');",
                  "  pm.expect(v, 'dryRunVisitId (run the dry-run queue first)').to.be.a('number');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('400 rejected', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('error names the unknown field', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include('unknown_field'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Wrong key -> 401",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rpa-derm-queue",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rpa-derm-queue"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Overrides the collection auth with a wrong x-rpa-key to show the endpoint is secured. Expect 401.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "apikey",
              "apikey": [
                {
                  "key": "key",
                  "value": "x-rpa-key",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "value",
                  "value": "deliberately-wrong-key",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "in",
                  "value": "header",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}